      "human_comment": "",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "14.Nce2 is the most accurate move, maintaining White's advantage (+0.60, Stockfish:16). After [pv:Nce2 Nc5 Nxd4 Bd7 Ngf3], Black immediately has a hanging piece, and pressuring weak enemy material is a practical way to keep the initiative. In return, the line may allow Black to improve the pawn structure and shed the doubled pawns. Nb1 is a comparable option that also leads to a slight advantage for White via [pv:Nb1 Nc6 Nf3 Nc5 Nbd2], setting up renewed knight activity much as the game later unfolded.",
