      "human_comment": "",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "Black's 23...fxg4 leads to a slight advantage for White (+0.67, Stockfish:16), yet it creates a passed pawn on g4\u2014a forward unit that can tie down defenders\u2014and opens the f-file for the rook. The main continuation is [pv:fxg4 Rcg1 g3 Rxg3 Na6]. As a comparable option, 23...Na6 leads to a clear advantage for White [pv:Na6 a3 Rxc1 Rxc1 Rc8], targeting the rook on c1 and potentially leaving a White piece hanging further along, but fxg4 keeps White's edge narrower.",
