      "human_comment": "?!  With this move Lilienthal loses his advantage. \nStronger and perhaps decisive was 25. Rxg4 and if 25... Rcf8 then 26. Rh4 with\nthe idea of calling the Knight to help with the maneuver Nd4-f3-h2-g4.",
      "human_symbol": null,
      "system_comment": "White missed the potential to put Black's king under pressure and activate the rooks on the open files, as 25.Bxg4 lets the advantage slip away to equality (+0.77 \u2192 +0.14, Stockfish:16) [pv:Bxg4 Rxf4 Rcf1 Rxf1 Rxf1] and the continuation may leave White with a hanging piece. Rxg4 leads to a clear advantage for White [pv:Rxg4 Kg7 Rh4 Rcf8 Rch1].",
