      "system_comment": "Rather than 26...Rxf4, which leads to a slight advantage for White while winning a pawn and putting immediate pressure on White's king, 26...h5 makes matters worse\u2014White now has a clear advantage (+0.27 \u2192 +0.77, Stockfish:16) [pv:h5 gxh6 g5 Rg1 gxf4+]. The h-pawn thrust targets the bishop on g4, and Black's rook may eventually get behind the passed pawn, but in return White's king could become safer and a passed pawn on h6 may emerge. 26...Rxf4 was a comparable option, leading to a slight advantage for White [pv:Rxf4 Rxf4 Rxf4 Rg1 Rf8].",
